{
  "about": "Speeding speech up or slowing it down without changing its pitch. Input: a test tone (fundamental f0 Hz plus harmonics with the given amplitudes, loudness swelling at swellHz, normalized to peak 1) of `seconds` at `sampleRate`, and a speed factor (2 = twice as fast). Checks, measured away from the first and last 0.2 s: the output's length is the input's divided by the factor; its pitch (rising zero crossings per second) is f0; and its largest sample-to-sample jump is no bigger than the input's (no clicks at the joins). Also how long it may take.",
